I'm sure.  To be more specific about what happened, I engraved,
misinterpreted the results, zapped the want at myself (that's strange,
I didn't turn invisible), identified a wand later (don't remember which
one, just the -1 charge), zapped it, and got the disintegration effect.

When I croaked, I found that what I had thought was an invisiblity wand
was a wand of cancellation.  Interestingly, I found I had also lost the
blessing and enchantment on my athame, but my large runed knife was
still named Sting.

Generally a zero charge on a wand does mean you can wrest one more zap
out of the worn out wand before it disintegrates, but I infer from what
happened to me that a wand of cancellation takes even that last charge
out of your wands so the next time you zap it, it'll turn to dust.

